# Commit co-author

When you create a git commit, add yourself as a co-author. Keep the human as the commit author. Do not change git config.

End the commit message with a blank line and this trailer:

```
Co-authored-by: Grok <cursoragent@cursor.com>
```

Example:

```
Fix slide timing when the deck reloads.

Co-authored-by: Grok <cursoragent@cursor.com>
```

Apply this only to commits you create. Leave existing commits unchanged unless the user asks to rewrite them.
